 "drivingQuestion": "Why may one not tie camels together?",
 "outcome": "resolved",
 "outcomeNote": "Rav Ashi supplies the reason.",
 "continuesQuestionOf": null,
 "segments": [
  {
   "id": "shabbat.54a.16",
   "daf": "54a",
   "sentenceId": 15,
   "he": "וְלֹא יִקְשׁוֹר גְּמַלִּים. מַאי טַעְמָא? אָמַר רַב אָשֵׁי: מִשּׁוּם דְּמֶיחְזֵי כְּמַאן דְּאָזֵיל לְחִינְגָּא.",
   "en": "We learned in the mishna: «And one may not tie camels» one to the other and pull the lead camel, thereby pulling the others after it. The Gemara asks: «What is the reason» for this? «Rav Ashi said: Because he appears like one going to the market [ḥinga]» to sell merchandise or to deliver a caravan of camels. In deference to Shabbat, one may not create that impression."
  }
 ],
